            <div xml:id="d304">

                <pb facs="0416" n="321" xml:id="pg321"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/8203a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dickover</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-09-30T18:00:00-05:00">September 30, 1936—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>125. 1. Associated Press despatch from Tokyo states that rejection by the Cabinet
                    of extensive administrative reforms advocated by the army and navy might lead to
                    the resignation of the Minister of War and consequently result in resignation of
                    the entire Cabinet.</p>
                <p>2. Having in mind recent developments in Sino-Japanese relations, your comments
                    by telegraph on the subject of the above-mentioned press report would be of
                    interest.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
